# Start here (slabitz agent root)

You are in `@ROOT@`. Read only below this folder. This file is generated by
`dev-root init` from `tools/AGENT_START.md.in`; do not edit it here.

## Do this first

```
cd @ROOT@/wt/<task>             # your worktree (the reviewer made it: dev-root new <task>)
. @ROOT@/env.sh                 # environment, data variables, sbz, gpu-run (TMPDIR follows the worktree)
sbz where                       # check: key, kernel sets, data paths
```

Then read `AGENTS.md`, `docs/dev/README.md` and your task file
`docs/dev/Tnn_*.md` in the worktree.

## Layout

| Path | What | You may |
|---|---|---|
| `wt/<task>/` | your git worktree (branch `<task>`) | read, write, commit |
| `tmp/<task>/` | your `TMPDIR` (`env.sh` sets it) | read, write |
| `kernels/<srckey>/` | built kernel sets, keyed by kernel sources; `sbz build` publishes here | read (only `sbz` writes) |
| `data/real/` | real detector files (symlinks, read-only) and `INVENTORY.md` | read |
| `data/synth/current/` | synthetic data (T00) | read |
| `data/compat/`, `toolchains/` | zstd versions and corpus (T07) | read |
| `ext/` | pac-zstd (`$PAC_LIB`), bslz4_to_sparse | read |
| `main/` | origin/main, kept current by the reviewer | read |
| `env/`, `shared/`, `admin/`, `bin/`, `repo.git/` | environment, slangc, tools | do not touch |
| `results/` | benchmark outputs | write only through `sbz gate` |

## Commands

```
sbz build                  kernels linked from the cache when the sources match, library built here (seconds)
sbz test                   the regression tests (each under timeout)
gpu-run sbz test           the same on an idle Slurm L40S; ALL timing goes through gpu-run
sbz build-sm35 / build-fatbins    old-card and portable kernel sets (cached the same way)
sbz where                  paths in use
```

## Rules

- Never run pixi, pip or conda. Never download anything. No network.
- Write only in your worktree and `tmp/<task>`. Never write in `data/`, `main/`, `env/`,
  `shared/`, `ext/`, `toolchains/` or `kernels/` by hand.
- Do not search the filesystem for test data: use `$SLABITZ_EXAMPLES` (`data/real`) and
  `$SLABITZ_SYNTH`. `data/real/INVENTORY.md` says what each file is.
- Never read or write outside this folder, not even `/tmp` (use `$TMPDIR`). Workers started by
  opencode with this folder as working directory must use RELATIVE paths (`wt/<task>/...`): an
  absolute path to the same folder is treated as outside it and auto-rejected.
- If a package or tool is missing: write the need to `QUESTIONS.txt` in your worktree,
  finish what does not depend on it, and stop. The reviewer changes the shared environment.
- Never push. The user does all pushes.
- Report: `docs/dev/reports/Tnn.md` in your worktree, as the task file says.
